# FIFO Elapsed Timer

## Purpose

The timer measures the time between a FIFO write and a FIFO read.

## Operation

### Start

A FIFO write generates:

```text
start = 1
```

The timer is reset:

```text
seconds = 0
```

and begins counting.

### Count

For a 100 MHz clock:

```text
100,000,000 clock cycles = 1 second
```

The timer increments once per second.

### Stop

A FIFO read generates:

```text
stop = 1
```

The timer stops at its current value.

## Example

```text
BTNU
 ↓
FIFO WRITE
 ↓
Timer = 00
 ↓
01
 ↓
02
 ↓
03
 ↓
BTNC
 ↓
FIFO READ
 ↓
Timer STOP
```

The timer therefore measures approximately three seconds.

## Display

The timer value is shown as a four-digit decimal value:

```text
0000
0001
0002
...
0099
```

The current implementation saturates at 99 seconds.
